      Concept   : NXmpes/ENTRY/DATA/kx  [OPTIONAL]
      Inheritance:
        NXmpes/ENTRY/DATA/kx
          Doc       : Calibrated k-space coordinate in x direction. It is envisioned that the axes
                      in momentum space are named ``kx``, ``ky``, and ``kz``. Typically, the vectors
                      in momentum space are defined such that ``kx`` and ``ky`` comprise the
                      parallel component, while ``kz`` is the perpendicular component. It is also
                      possible to define ``k_parallel`` and ``k_perp`` for the parallel and
                      perpendicular momenta, respectively. Units are typically 1/angstrom.
